# MCP POLICY — ShoppyFender

Project root is always `/Volumes/TimeData/Cursor/ShoppyFender`. Do not use `~/Developer/ShopyFender`.

1. Use Godot MCP for inspecting, running and modifying Godot scenes when it provides a clear advantage over direct file editing.
2. Use Blender MCP only for 3D modeling, materials, scene inspection and asset-generation tasks.
3. Use Context7 when implementing version-sensitive Godot APIs or external library APIs.
4. Prefer local Git commands for commits, diffs, branches, push and pull.
5. Use GitHub MCP only for GitHub-specific remote operations such as issues, pull requests and repository metadata. Do not treat it as required.
6. Do not install new MCP servers without explicit approval.
7. Do not call paid generation services automatically (Higgsfield, Hyper3D, Hunyuan3D, and similar credit APIs).
8. Never expose access tokens in source files, prompts or logs.
9. Never perform destructive GitHub operations without explicit approval.
10. Keep all game runtime code independent from MCP.

Godot MCP requires the Godot editor open on this project with the Godot MCP plugin enabled (port 6505). Blender MCP requires the Blender addon enabled and **Start MCP Server** clicked in the viewport N-panel (port 9876).
